  "question": "A train moving at 20 m/s applies brakes and stops after 10 seconds. Calculate retardation.",
  "gold_answer": "# Solved Numerical\n\n---\n\n## Kinematics Problem\n\n### Problem\nA train moving at $20 \\text{ m/s}$ applies brakes and stops after $10 \\text{ seconds}$. Calculate retardation.\n\n### Given\n* Initial velocity ($u$) = $20 \\text{ m/s}$\n* Final velocity ($v$) = $0 \\text{ m/s}$ (since it stops)\n* Time taken ($t$) = $10 \\text{ s}$\n\n### Formula\n$$a = \\frac{v - u}{t}$$\n\n### Substitution\n$$a = \\frac{0 - 20}{10}$$\n\n### Calculation\n$$a = \\frac{-20}{10}$$\n\n$$a = -2 \\text{ m/s}^2$$\n\nRetardation is the magnitude of negative acceleration:\n$$\\text{Retardation} = -a$$\n\n### Final Answer\n**Retardation = $2 \\text{ m/s}^2$**\n\n### Interpretation\nThis indicates that the brakes cause the train's velocity to decrease uniformly at a steady rate of $2 \\text{ meters per second}$ every single second until it reaches a complete standstill.",
  "candidate_response": "┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Problem Overview**                                              │\n│                                                                   │\n│ A train undergoes uniform deceleration (retardation) from an      │\n│ initial velocity to a complete standstill over a specific time    │\n│ interval.                                                         │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Given Parameters**                                              │\n│                                                                   │\n│ • **Initial Velocity ($u$):** $20\\text{ m/s}$                     │\n│ • **Final Velocity ($v$):** $0\\text{ m/s}$ (The train stops)      │\n│ • **Time Interval ($t$):** $10\\text{ s}$                          │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Main Formula: Acceleration**                                    │\n│                                                                   │\n│ $$a = \\frac{v - u}{t}$$                                           │\n│                                                                   │\n│ **[ Explain Formula ]**                                           │\n│ This formula defines acceleration as the rate of change of        │\n│ velocity over time. A negative result indicates retardation.      │\n│                                                                   │\n│ **[ Open Formula Lab ]**                                          │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Step-by-Step Calculation**                                      │\n│                                                                   │\n│ 1. **Identify Variables:**                                        │\n│    $u = 20$, $v = 0$, $t = 10$                                    │\n│                                                                   │\n│ 2. **Substitute into Formula:**                                   │\n│    $a = \\frac{0 - 20}{10}$                                        │\n│                                                                   │\n│ 3. **Solve for $a$:**                                             │\n│    $a = \\frac{-20}{10} = -2\\text{ m/s}^2$                         │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Key Concepts: Acceleration vs. Retardation**                    │\n│                                                                   │\n| Term         | Value             | Direction                      |\n|--------------|-------------------|--------------------------------|\n| Acceleration | $-2\\text{ m/s}^2$ | Opposite to motion             |\n| Retardation  | $2\\text{ m/s}^2$  | Magnitude of slowing down      |\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Final Answer**                                                  │\n│                                                                   │\n│ The retardation of the train is **$2\\text{ m/s}^2$**.             │\n│                                                                   │\n│ *(Note: Retardation is the absolute value of negative             │\n│ acceleration.)*                                                   │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ **Suggested Questions**                                           │\n│                                               